<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $30 mln Dec 11.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $30 mln Dec 11.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $30 million surplus on December 11 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 11</p>
<p>Exports: $171.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $247.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $349.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $243.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $30 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.611 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.590 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.500 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.470 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.051 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
